# Form-Native JIT Track

Goal: the optimizer is fully Form-native and witnessed, with no new runtime
meaning living in C lowering. The C seed may carry host install/call plumbing
while it shrinks, but this track treats Form recipes, Form emitters, and Form
receipts as the source of truth. A number beside a band is its `./fkwu` verdict,
every one of them the band's full answer.

## Invariants

- The optimizer proper is Form: decide, profile, specialize, lower, guard,
  deopt, melt, and witness.
- The walker remains the semantic oracle. Every native specialization needs a
  parity witness or a named pending receipt.
- Per-instance observations collapse into stable numeric categories before
  they guide native code.
- A specialization carries a guard, fallback, and deopt/melt receipt.
- Form source passes a static analyzer gate for facts that can be proven
  before execution or JIT lowering: missing source attribution, unbound symbols,
  arity mismatches, literal div/mod by zero, literal bounds faults, and static
  null/empty dereferences.
- A direct native access preserves runtime fault semantics: bounds checks,
  null/nothing checks, div/mod-by-zero checks, type/shape checks, and structured
  exceptions with stack trace plus file/line/column/span attribution.
- Container access is not claimed direct unless the representation receipt proves
  the access path: cons head/tail, indexed buffer/vector, dict/hash bucket, or
  ordered tree path.
- CPU/GPU register wins are claims only after a Form emitter/witness names the
  register lane, spill/rooting behavior, and parity result.
- Numeric tags that cross JIT cells have one Form name at their first owner;
  container operation tags live in `model/jit-container-lowering.fk`.
- The native path for a recipe is generated from the recipe itself on demand
  (`docs/form-agent-active-contribution.md`); there is no operations table to
  keep in step.

## What runs — crystallize on heat

- **The heat lane.** `observe/jit-evaluator-heat.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-evaluator-heat-band.fk` 4095) counts heat on the
  evaluator's leaves; `form/form-stdlib/jit-heat-gate.fk`
  (`form/form-stdlib/tests/jit-heat-gate-band.fk` 4095) decides what
  crystallizes; hot leaves crystallize native and melt on cool.
  `observe/lane-counsel-run.fk` (rows in `form/form-stdlib/lane-counsel.bml`,
  `lane-counsel-band` 2047) judges the performance lanes worst-first and names
  each lane's stone.
- **The loop lane.** A loop-shaped recipe crystallizes transparently: lets,
  if-chains, calls, self recursion, closures, higher-order arguments, cons and
  list doors, string slots (byte reads, equality, building, templates) and float
  heads each have a band under `form/form-stdlib/tests/loop-lane-*-band.fk`, all
  twenty answering in full (`loop-lane-call-band` 8191,
  `loop-lane-string-door-band` 2047, `loop-lane-cons-band` 511, ...). Its
  admit/pulse/emit arms (`fk_f64_*`) live in `runtime/fkwu-uni.c`.
- **Form lowering.** `form/form-stdlib/form-lower.fk` lowers recipes to machine
  bytes in Form, strings included: compile-time strings embed, and a runtime
  haystack and a runtime needle+`from` cross through the two-slot
  `fk_inram_args` convention (`release-ledger.bml` R10/R28/R34;
  `form-lower-string-band` 63, `form-lower-string-runtime-band` 255,
  `form-lower-string-both-runtime-band` 511).
- **The GPU lane.** `form/form-stdlib/bml/gpu-lower.bml` reads a defn's own
  nodes through `kernel_ast` and emits one Metal kernel — reduce, map, filter,
  any/all, or a one-thread walk — admitted by content, one enqueue per call
  (`gpu-lower-band` 1048575). `form/form-stdlib/bml/gpu-dispatch.bml` lets
  representation choose: a resident tensor takes the GPU, a list stays on the
  CPU lane, and callers never name the lane (`gpu-dispatch-band` 63).
- **Metal pipelines** are emitted from Form at runtime
  (`native-tensor-lifecycle-band` 1023, `jit-metal-lanes-band` 8191,
  `metal-handle-door-band` 65535).

## The policy spine (Form, witnessed)

- Profile receipt shape and numeric category collapse —
  `observe/jit-profile-receipt.fk` (`observe/tests/jit-profile-receipt-band.fk`
  127): per-instance receipts collapse to category signatures; masks name
  crystallize, inline, stack, field, index, hash, tree, CPU, and GPU eligibility.
- Category-fed tiering — `observe/jit-tier-policy.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-tier-policy-band.fk` 1023): receipts choose
  baseline/profile, hold, crystallize, specialize, deopt, or melt.
- Runtime checks and source-attributed exceptions — `observe/jit-runtime-fault.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-runtime-fault-band.fk` 511): bounds, null-ref, div/mod by
  zero, type/shape, and parity-checkable exception receipts with stack trace and
  full source attribution.
- Inlining and call tracking — `observe/jit-inline-policy.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-inline-policy-band.fk` 1023): monomorphic calls inline,
  low-polymorphic calls need a guarded inline, megamorphic calls fall back.
- Static analyzer pre-execution gate — `observe/form-static-analyzer.fk`
  (`observe/tests/form-static-analyzer-band.fk` 16383).
- Stack and frame collapse — `observe/jit-stack-frame.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-stack-frame-band.fk` 255).
- Representation specialization (field, array/list, dict/hashmap, ordered map) —
  `observe/jit-representation-specialization.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-representation-specialization-band.fk` 1023).
- CPU register / SIMD and GPU register / memory lowering —
  `observe/jit-register-lowering.fk` (`observe/tests/jit-register-lowering-band.fk` 511).
- Deopt, melt, invalidation, and code cache — `observe/jit-deopt-cache.fk`
  (`observe/tests/jit-deopt-cache-band.fk` 511); the grouped sweep
  `observe/tests/jit-policy-front-sweep-band.fk` 31.
- Emitter bundle, native IR, host dispatch, backend emission, loader contract —
  `observe/jit-emitter-bundle.fk` 8191, `observe/jit-native-ir.fk` 16383,
  `observe/jit-host-dispatch.fk` 8191, `observe/jit-backend-emission.fk` 8191,
  `observe/jit-loader-contract.fk` 16383, each through its
  `observe/tests/<name>-band.fk`.
- Native dispatch and witness sweeps — `observe/jit-native-dispatch-sweep.fk`
  16383, `observe/jit-full-track-sweep.fk` 536870911,
  `observe/jit-native-witness-sweep.fk` 67108863,
  `observe/jit-self-host-completion-sweep.fk` 134217727,
  `observe/jit-runtime-stack-attribution.fk` 2047.

## The dylib bridge (the intended live-execution path)

Form owns the JIT semantics — source lowering, container byte payloads, guards,
exception/deopt/melt/parity routes, generation, source maps — and the host
carrier is treated as a callable native path only after all of them pass:

- `observe/jit-dylib-cache-lifecycle.fk` — 16777215
- `observe/jit-dylib-call-dispatch-evidence.fk` — 134217727
- `observe/jit-dylib-call-result-evidence.fk` — 134217727
- `observe/jit-dylib-invoke-return-evidence.fk` — 268435455
- `observe/jit-dylib-live-proof-suite.fk` — 536870911
- `observe/tests/jit-dylib-live-runtime-proof-band.fk` — 4294967295
- `observe/jit-rung20-dylib-runtime-audit.fk` — 268435455
- `model/jit-source-runtime-orchestrator.fk` — 1048575
- the container pipeline — `model/jit-container-lowering.fk` 16383,
  `model/jit-container-backend.fk` 65535, `model/jit-container-byteplan.fk` 65535,
  `model/jit-container-loader.fk` 65535, `model/jit-container-source-runtime.fk`
  65535, `model/jit-container-profile-runtime.fk` 65535,
  `model/jit-container-replacement-runtime.fk` 255,
  `model/jit-container-live-slot-runtime.fk` 1048575,
  `model/jit-source-dylib-container-executor.fk` 4194303,
  `model/jit-self-host-container-runtime-loop.fk` 1048575,
  `model/jit-self-host-container-live-evidence.fk` 4194303, each through its
  `model/tests/<name>-band.fk`
- the live bridge and gates — `observe/jit-source-replacement-runtime.fk`
  536870911, `observe/jit-final-native-gate.fk` 8388607,
  `observe/jit-live-execution-evidence.fk` 536870911,
  `observe/jit-live-runtime-integration.fk` 67108863,
  `observe/jit-rung20-readiness.fk` 536870911,
  `observe/jit-host-membrane-current-gate.fk` 33554431,
  `observe/jit-dylib-live-runtime-container-gate.fk` 134217727,
  `observe/jit-slot-runtime-fault-bridge.fk` 1048575
- the POSIX W^X carrier lives in `runtime/fkwu-uni.c` (the seed's install path;
  a shrink candidate like the rest of the seed).

## Where it is going

- **The last rung.** Full Form-native JIT witnessed: hot source recipes lower
  through the Form-owned IR / backend bundles / byte streams into the host
  install/call membrane, dispatch native, throw source-attributed runtime
  exceptions, deopt/melt safely, and pass the native witness sweep — without
  C lowering as the optimizer source. Rung 20's readiness audit
  (`observe/jit-rung20-readiness.fk`) composes only current receipts.
- **The loop lane comes home to Form.** Its admit, pulse and emit arms are the
  live JIT most recipes meet, and they are C. Lowering the same loop shapes
  through `form-lower.fk`, as `gpu-lower.bml` already does for the GPU, moves
  that meaning out of the seed.
- **Heat reaches Form lowering.** `jit-heat-gate.fk` does not yet name
  `form-lower`'s string family as something to crystallize on heat, so
  `str_find`'s Form crystallization is not reached from a live hot call site.
